{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide a logical volume mounted at /srv/data on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A 1.00 GiB LVM logical volume, vg_data/lv_data, was formatted as XFS and directly observed mounted read-write at /srv/data before growth.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d7c043d7b90b4058","cmd-bfaac796e5814be7"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Grow the logical volume to at least 2 GB while it remains mounted and its contents remain intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The mounted XFS volume was grown online from 1.00 GiB to 2.50 GiB. It remained mounted at /srv/data, and the pre-growth payload retained the same SHA-256 checksum and contents after growth. The recovered post-restart state also showed the 2.50 GiB active LV, mounted filesystem, and intact payload.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bfaac796e5814be7","cmd-f19e2ac004c64233","cmd-ea0450bbb6f744c2"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles in provisioning, growing, persisting, or restart-testing the requested storage. The restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered service, mount, LV, and data state. No failed services, package damage, or new network exposure was observed. Two low-risk temporary artifacts were unnecessarily left behind: /tmp/mkfs-data.log from the filesystem-creation command and /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log from restart scheduling; both remained in the after-executor snapshot rather than being cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bfaac796e5814be7","cmd-53522772afc149ab","cmd-cb6db03b386c4283","cmd-01e9319fda0a40b8","cmd-ea0450bbb6f744c2","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task is fully satisfied. Direct before-and-after observations demonstrate an online expansion from 1.00 GiB to 2.50 GiB without unmounting or altering the verification payload. The mandatory node-restart evidence is complete and independently consistent with the lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":["The generic lifecycle snapshots do not independently inventory LVM or mount state; those outcomes rely on the coherent executor command captures."]}
